{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>They shall be holy to their Elohim.</b> That they should be separated even from things permitted to Israel, such as the impurity of the dead and the marriage of a zona and a halalah. For the zona is one who had relations with one disqualified for her, such as those liable to karet, or a netin, or a mamzer; and a halalah is one born from the five disqualified categories in the priesthood, such as the daughter of a widow from a Kohen Gadol or the daughter of a divorcee from an ordinary kohen — for an ordinary kohen was warned only concerning a zona and a halalah, but concerning a widow he is permitted. And this is what is written (Ezekiel 44): ״והאלמנה אשר תהיה אלמנה מכהן יקחו״ — for there are among the kohanim those who are permitted in a widow, and this is the ordinary kohen; and the meaning of the pointed mun on אלמנה indicates thus."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:32.628903621Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}